# Coding Rules — Multi-AI Orchestrator Extension
# Author: Sohel Ahammad
# Version: 4.0.0
# These rules apply to ALL files in this extension.

---

## RULE-01: No NPM Dependencies in Runtime Code
- NEVER add packages to `dependencies` in package.json
- All HTTP calls use Node.js built-in `https` module only
- All file operations use Node.js built-in `fs` and `path`
- `devDependencies` are allowed (eslint, @types/vscode) but never bundled
- REASON: VSIX must stay lean; no node_modules folder in package

## RULE-02: All API Keys from VSCode Settings ONLY
- NEVER hardcode any API key, token, or secret in any file
- NEVER log API keys to console or write to any file
- Keys MUST come from: `vscode.workspace.getConfiguration('multiAI').get('...')`
- ECC scanner MUST block any PR that introduces raw key patterns

## RULE-03: Every Async Call Has Timeout + Error Boundary
- ALL `httpPost()` calls MUST use `timeoutMs` parameter (default: 30000ms)
- ALL orchestrator steps MUST be wrapped in try/catch
- Parallel steps MUST use `Promise.allSettled()` — never `Promise.all()`
- REASON: One failing provider must never crash the entire pipeline

## RULE-04: Webview Lifecycle — Zero Memory Leaks
- EVERY `setInterval` MUST be stored and cleared in `onDidDispose`
- EVERY `fs.watch` MUST be stored and `.close()`d in `onDidDispose`
- EVERY `fs.watchFile` MUST be `fs.unwatchFile()`d in `onDidDispose`
- Use `let` for all watcher/interval references, set to `null` after clearing
- PATTERN: Guard every cleanup with `if (ref) { cleanup; ref = null; }`

## RULE-05: Content Security Policy — No unsafe-eval
- ALL webview panels MUST use nonce-based CSP:
  `script-src 'nonce-${nonce}'` — generated via `crypto.randomBytes(16)`
- NEVER use `'unsafe-eval'` or `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts
- Inline styles (`style-src 'unsafe-inline'`) are acceptable for webviews

## RULE-06: Regex Patterns Must Be Recreated Per Call
- NEVER store regex with `/g` flag as a class property and reuse it
- CORRECT: create a new regex inside the function: `const re = /pattern/g`
- WRONG: `this.pattern = /sk-[a-z]+/g` then `this.pattern.test(code)` repeatedly
- REASON: `/g` flag retains `lastIndex` state — causes false negatives

## RULE-07: SVG Laser Coordinates After DOM Paint
- NEVER calculate SVG line coordinates synchronously on mount
- ALWAYS use double `requestAnimationFrame` before reading `getBoundingClientRect()`
- Pattern: `requestAnimationFrame(() => requestAnimationFrame(() => positionAgents()))`
- Recalculate on `window.resize`
- Set SVG `viewBox` to match stage pixel dimensions exactly

## RULE-08: Status File — Always Use Error Boundary
- `JSON.parse()` on `.ai_team_status.json` MUST be in try/catch
- On any error, return `getDefaultStatus()` — never throw
- Never read the file synchronously during a write operation
- Check `fs.existsSync()` before reading

## RULE-09: Theme — Use VSCode CSS Variables in Sidebar
- Sidebar HTML MUST NOT contain any hardcoded dark-theme colors
- ALWAYS use: `var(--vscode-sideBar-background)`, `var(--vscode-button-background)`, etc.
- HUD (Round-Table) is intentionally always dark — exception allowed with comment
- Provide fallback values: `var(--vscode-button-background, #2563eb)`

## RULE-10: Multi-Root Workspace Support
- NEVER use `vscode.workspace.rootPath` (deprecated)
- ALWAYS iterate `vscode.workspace.workspaceFolders` when searching for files
- Check if the file exists in each folder before returning its path
- If not found in any folder, create in `folders[0]`

## RULE-11: New Files Must Be Added to build-vsix.js
- When adding a new `.js` file to `extention/`, IMMEDIATELY add it to `filesToCopy`
  in `build-vsix.js`
- Rebuild and verify the VSIX file count increases
- REASON: Missing files cause silent `require()` crashes at activation

## RULE-12: Commands Must Have Keyboard Shortcuts
- Every primary command MUST have a keybinding in `package.json`
- Follow pattern: `Ctrl+Alt+[letter]` / `Cmd+Alt+[letter]` for Mac
- Document shortcuts in sidebar HTML and README

## RULE-13: User-Facing Errors Must Be Helpful
- NEVER show raw JavaScript errors to users
- Error messages MUST include: what failed + how to fix it
- For missing API keys: always offer "Open Settings" action button
- For timeout: mention which provider failed and suggest fallback

## RULE-14: No Polling — Use fs.watch + Heartbeat
- NEVER use `fs.watchFile` as the primary sync mechanism (polling-based)
- PREFER `fs.watch` (event-based) with `fs.watchFile` as fallback only
- HUD sends 400ms ping → extension pushes status (heartbeat pattern)
- Maximum poll interval if fallback needed: 300ms

## RULE-15: Documentation Must Stay Current
- PRD.md, PHASES.md, DESIGN.md, ARCHITECTURE.md must be updated with every release
- CHANGELOG.md must have an entry for every version bump
- Version in package.json, CHANGELOG.md, and extension title must match
- .RULES must be updated when new patterns are established
